y Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Culture and Leisure Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Rural and Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"South Kesteven forecasts budget deficits from 2027/28 as government funding falls","lead":"South Kesteven District Council faces structural deficits from 2027/28 onwards as government funding reduces over a three-year settlement period, according to papers reviewed by the Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee. While a one-off grant mitigates funding losses in 2026/27, the council has no guarantee of additional support in future years, the papers state. The deficit forecast will require the council to cut spending to balance its budget. Separately, the council's housing account faces pressure from an unsustainable capital programme that will significantly reduce reserves over three years, forcing a fundamental review of investment priorities using stock condition data. The building control partnership that South Kesteven runs with two other councils showed improved financial performance, with fee income \u00a321,000 above budget, though Rushcliffe Borough Council reported a deficit while the other two partners showed surpluses.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"AppendixBHRAFinanceRiskRegister202627","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52493/52493.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Direct Debit Error","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52574/52574.pdf","headline":"Council acknowledges customers spreading August payment over remaining year could have detrimental impact on collection rates","detail":"1,594 customers (4.4% of those adversely affected) chose to spread their August instalment over the remainder of the financial year rather than pay by alternative methods. The council explicitly states this could have a detrimental impact on collection rates.","category":"income","matters":"Changes to collection timing of major revenue sources affect cash flow predictability and require adjusted financial forecasting","figures":"1,594 customers (4.4% of affected customers)","quote":"There could be a detrimental impact on the collection rates for Council Tax income where customers have chosen to spread the August instalment over the remainder of the financial year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Direct Debit Error","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52574/52574.pdf","headline":"Single-officer responsibility with no independent verification caused processing date not to be changed from system default, creating control weakness","detail":"The error resulted from one officer failing to change the system default processing date from 28 July to 31 July, with no independent check on this critical input before file upload. Once uploaded, the file could not be corrected. The council has now introduced a new procedure requiring the process to be checked by two revenue team leaders and the head of service, with all checks to be completed same-day.","category":"governance","matters":"Single points of failure in critical financial processes indicate control discipline issues; lenders assess this when evaluating financial management capability","figures":"Processing date defaulted to 28 July instead of being changed to 31 July","quote":"One of the main reasons for the error was that the checking of the processing date was not undertaken by a different officer and was within the responsibility of one officer only.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Council Tax Direct Debit Error","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52574/52574.pdf","headline":"\u00a36.5m Council Tax revenue collected on 29 July instead of 3 August forced recalculation of cashflow projections for remainder of financial year","detail":"An administrative error in setting the direct debit processing date led to 36,079 customers having their August instalment called on 29 July instead of the correct date of 3 August. This early collection of \u00a36.5m interrupted the council's cashflow forecasts, which had to be recalculated.","category":"income","matters":"Disruptions to cashflow forecasts affect a council's liquidity management capability and its ability to meet operational and financial obligations; lenders assess financial forecasting reliability","figures":"\u00a36.5m, called 29 July instead of 3 August, affecting 36,079 customers","quote":"The cashflow projections of the Council have been interrupted by the early call of Direct Debit income which has resulted in the cashflow projections for the remainder of the year to be recalculated.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Internal Audit Follow Up Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52571/52571.pdf","headline":"Building Control KPI dashboard implementation is 14 months overdue with completion date uncertain.","detail":"A requirement to implement a Building Control KPI dashboard consolidating inspection booking reliability, website request completion, contact responsiveness and slot adherence was due 31 July 2025. As of September 2026 it remains incomplete. Management notes the development is 'dependent on support from other Council departments' and 'an expected completion date cannot currently be confirmed', with a revised target of 31 October 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"Slippage in basic management information systems for a traded service signals either resource constraints or weak project governance that could affect operational performance and service revenue.","figures":"Originally due 31/07/2025; rescheduled to 31/10/2026 \u2014 14 months overdue","quote":"Development remains dependent on support from other Council departments and, as a result, an expected completion date cannot currently be confirmed.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","paper_title":"Stock Audit \u2013 Update","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52572/52572.pdf","headline":"Council implementing Stock and Go automated van inventory system beginning September 2026","detail":"Under a new contract with Huws Gray, the council is deploying Stock and Go for van stock management, providing automated replenishment, live inventory visibility, and instant job costing. Repairs and Voids managers are mobilising the system in September-October 2026.","category":"other","matters":"This represents investment in technical controls to prevent stock loss and improve operational visibility, complementing governance improvements.","figures":"Stock and Go implementation scheduled for September-October 2026","quote":"The Council have already started to receive improved usage and spend reports each month as part of the new contract which will be supplemented with the introduction of Stock and Go.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"South Kesteven","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Additional staffing and rent collection software deployed to improve tenant arrears recovery","lead":"Tenant arrears collection rate directly affects HRA cash position and determines whether business plan income assumptions are met","also":["17 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Governance and Audit Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":18,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","top_paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":85,"news_drafts_total":1}}